{#- The scene-break decision item's context (`scene_break.build_item`), which
    `decide/user.j2` shows above the question. Vars:
      title — the scene's own title, so a proposed NEXT title is not a
              restatement of the one already on screen. "" when untitled.
      facts — dict from chronicle.scene_facts(): location (str), date (str),
              cast ([str] of "<kind>/<id>" refs). In for the same reason
              rolling_summary/user.j2 carries it: a scene's FIRST location and
              FIRST date are set silently (scenes/moment.py), so on the scenes
              that never move — the ordinary ones — the transcript says
              neither.
      signals — [{kind, weight, detail}] from scene_break.evaluate: the
              deterministic reasons the question is being asked. Rendered as
              `detail` alone; kind and weight are the scorer's bookkeeping and
              mean nothing to a reader.
      transcript — str (see snippets/transcript.j2): the posts since this scene
              was last considered, NOT the whole scene. -#}
{%- include "snippets/scene_break_head.j2" -%}
{%- if signals -%}
You are being asked because:
{% for s in signals %}- {{ s.detail }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
The scene since it was last considered:

{{ transcript }}
